WEBVTT

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.660
Thank you, Yuma. Astral.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.590
My lifelong friends.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.270
I'm glad I was able...

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.630
...to enjoy the greatest Duel with you guys in my final moments.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.190
SHARK!!

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.910
Later...!

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.460
The Surface World's beginning to fade away.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.170
Yeah, it looks like the world's been saved from danger.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.220
But Yuma will now...

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.680
In any case, I thank you for lending me your strength.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:51.140
I suppose I've managed to repay my debt from before even a bit.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.190
Tron...

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.650
Farewell, Kazuma.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.440
Thank you, Tron.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.200
<i>Yuma...</i>

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.040
Huh...? Not, not... Where am...?

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.880
Tokunosuke-<i>kun</i>?!

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.130
Huh?

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.640
I... Yuma!

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.730
What happened to us...?

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.380
After we defeated Shark,

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.810
the Barian World fused with the Surface World,

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:44.570
causing the multiple souls trapped there to return to this world, I believe.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:50.240
This is... Oh yeah, I...

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.580
it seems Yuma and his friends managed to pull it off.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.590
Yes. But Yuma is probably...

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.130
Tokunosuke!

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.470
Yuma!

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.720
It's all thanks to you, or not!

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.880
So this means they all managed to return, right?

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.140
Yuma!

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.560
Yuma!

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:15.810
Guys!

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.270
Yuma!

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.520
Tetsuo!

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.480
Yuma!

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.030
Anna! Robin!

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.210
YUMA!

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:29.550
{marker}

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:33.730
WONDER WINGS, will you carry me...

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:38.970
...to an even brighter world, TAKE OFF!

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:50.660
The Duel that decides our fate,

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:54.840
now, show me your [Heart] CARD

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.660
Words aren't enough to satisfy

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.640
the feelings I want to express.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:14.660
Beside you, I've always been dreaming the same

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.910
Right now, with you

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.840
Oh - By facing each other,

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:28.920
... to create a new future, let's Shining Draw!

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.020
On WONDER WINGS, you carry me...

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:39.450
... don't let us ever untie our hands,

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.620
<i>Kattobing</i> from the sun...

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:54.200
... on to an even brighter world, TAKE OFF TO THE FUTURE!

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.300
Guys... You're all safe!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.840
I knew you'd be able to do it!

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.260
I believed in you, Yuma!

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.140
Yeah, it's all thanks to you guys.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.140
<i>"The Ceremonial Fight!! Yuma vs. Astral"</i>

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.190
Yuma... We won, right?

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:18.940
Haruto... I...

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.690
Yuma...

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.940
I'm so sorry, Haruto.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:24.950
Because of me, Kaito, Shark, and Rio all...

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.620
I couldn't save any of them... not one of them... during this battle.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.830
To me, dueling...
 What exactly is dueling supposed to mean?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.050
Yuma...

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:10.660
Yuma... Now that all 100 Numbers have been gathered,

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.830
it has just appeared before us.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:20.130
Within this card is carved the past and the future of the entire universe.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.550
The Numeron Code!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:26.340
It would seem that the time for us to fulfill our final ordeal has come.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:30.810
It is my mission to rewrite this Numeron Code.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:35.310
Rewriting the entire past and future...

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.270
Astral?!

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.230
The Barian World still exists.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:40.940
Don't tell me you...?!

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.610
I will destroy the Barian World.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.910
No way... Are you serious?

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:52.660
The Barian World is the root of all chaos.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.540
I cannot allow it to remain.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.210
Didn't we change the Astral World?!

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.170
Sacrificing other things won't give us a future!

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.220
Don't you understand that yet?!

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.550
If we continue to fight, we'll carve open a path to the future some day!

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.970
Are you going to just throw away that possibility?!

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.850
Then what reason have we been fighting up until now?!

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:20.150
Just what does this fight mean, then?!

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:23.400
My answer will not change.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:28.110
I will destroy the Barian World. That is my mission.

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:31.530
I won't let you... I won't let you do that!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.830
Then what will you do?

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.330
In that case... In that case, we'll duel!

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.330
You and I...?

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:44.170
You mean to bet the rewriting of the future with the Numeron Code on this duel?

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.170
That's right!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.550
I have all the Numbers under my control.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:52.180
There isn't a single person in this world who can defeat me.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.640
And you still intend to fight me?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.310
If I win, you'll obey me!

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.140
Very well. Then if I should win,

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.690
I will destroy the Barian World

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:08.360
and I shall erase every last memory you have concerning me.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.030
Understand?

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:12.990
Yeah!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:18.330
Then let's meet in front of the station plaza this evening.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.040
Huh?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.210
Where's Astral?

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.580
What's happening?

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.000
<i>Yuma...?</i>

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:35.810
<i>Astral... I need a deck that can beat him...</i>

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:43.150
<i>This will be the final duel I have with Astral, after all...</i>

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:51.200
<i>I can't believe the two of us never really understood each other...</i>

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.700
Astral.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.330
I was the one who sent you to Yuma.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.790
And you two accomplished some amazing things together.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.500
No, there is still more.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:11.220
I still have my mission left to use the Numeron Code.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:17.180
Whatever you decide to do, that will become your futures.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.180
And this all went according to your plan?

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.890
Well, that's hard to say.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.440
You must have realized it.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:26.690
That Yuma is...

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.820
Are you going to fight against him?

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.110
Yes, with all I've got.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.570
I gotta get myself together!

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:42.660
In my Duel with Astral, his deck will have all the Numbers and Hope.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.170
I'm certain he's going to...

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:57.010
My bad, my bad! I couldn't hit the breaks!

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.680
Anna! But why?!

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.970
To summarize...

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.480
You're going to Duel against Astral, right?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.940
It'll be a splendid banquet, right?

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.020
Or not!

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.860
We were worried!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.070
So we came to check on you!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.030
Y-You guys!

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.700
Man, they sure are making a big fuss up there!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.820
We're going to need lots of Duel Lunches!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.200
Stupid. Don't fuss. Don't fuss.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:25.920
But I wonder when Yuma started having so many friends...

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.920
For real. I guess he owes it to his duels, right?

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.210
Ah, that's right, Akari.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:36.380
Maybe you should try using dueling to find yourself a husband!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.890
G-Grandma!

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.180
Gosh!

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.520
But...dueling, huh?

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:45.430
Well, maybe it's not all bad.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.480
Why're you all together?

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:50.360
I'm busy trying to make my deck, ya know!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:54.780
And that's why we came here to give you our cards!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.240
Huh?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.320
To summarize, in Astral's deck...

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.530
...lie all the Numbers.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.200
And to battle against them...

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.580
...you'll need a powerful deck, right?

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.210
If you'd like, you can use our cards!

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:11.170
We want to fight Astral together!

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.460
You guys...

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.210
We all owe Astral so much, after all.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.590
What's wrong, Yuma? Use them!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:19.260
Or not!

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:20.300
Yuma!

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.350
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:23.680
Thanks, guys.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:29.190
But I want to try fighting this Duel with my own strength.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.650
Yeah, for this one Duel...

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:34.860
...there's no meaning to it if I don't fight on my own.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.360
<i>Yuma...</i>

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.110
Guess you're right.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:42.780
For you, it'll be the last time you get to duel with Astral!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.950
I get it, so go an' give him a good beatdown with your own style!

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:51.210
Right.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.920
But I'll fight alongside your feelings!

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:57.550
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.470
It's kinda strange.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:05.430
We used to walk this way when Astral was with us.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.930
Yuma?

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.390
Hey, Kotori...

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:14.520
You've always watched all our Duels up until now.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.940
That's why I'm going to tell this only to you.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.950
Yuma...

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:32.580
Have you finished building your deck?

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.300
Yeah. And it's perfect!

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.840
So those two are finally going to fight each other.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.800
I wonder what Yuma's thinking right now.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.510
It's him we're talking about. He's just gonna beat him down with all his strength.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.470
Good luck, Yuma!

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.140
I'm preying for you guys to have a good fight!

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.180
Not, not!

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.020
Try your best, too, Astral!

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.190
<i>They don't know...</i>

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.940
<i>...the true meaning behind this duel.</i>

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.530
Is that for real?

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:04.700
A very strange gravitational field has begun breaking through the skies above this city.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:09.200
I can say with complete certainty that the Numeron Code will manifest in this city first.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.870
Then could this Duel possibly be...?

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.540
I see... This duel's for that...

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.500
The Numeron Code.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.670
The ultimate card that lets one rewrite the past and the future.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:27.640
<i>I pray that we can use that power to bring back your lost soul...Kaito.</i>

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:31.520
So Yuma and Astral plan to use the Numeron Code?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:36.270
I'm not sure, but this Duel seems to be related to that.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.980
<i>Yuma, this moment has finally come.</i>

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:42.820
<i>Ever since I first met you,</i>

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:45.860
<i>I had a feeling this day would come eventually...</i>

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:50.910
<i>This will be my last duel with you.</i>

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.620
<i>Astral, ever since then...</i>

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.830
<i>I knew things would come to this eventually.</i>

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.300
<i>I just didn't think it'd happen like this.</i>

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.260
Let's begin, Yuma.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.300
Yeah, let's go!

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.300
I'm gonna bring it to ya!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.020
Duel Disk, set!

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:21.570
D-Gazer, set!

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.870
Duel Target...locked on!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.450
<i>AR Vision - Link established.</i>

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.750
Duel!!

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:44.550
The first turn's mine!
 My turn! Draw!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:50.470
<i>This is both my first and last duel against him!</i>

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.980
<i>Here I go, Astral.</i>

00:13:54.980 --> 00:14:01.400
I Summon Gogogo Golem in Attack Mode!

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:07.820
I then set three cards...ending my turn!

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:09.820
<i>Yuma...</i>

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:13.290
<i>Yuma, for you to dare place Gogogo Golem in Attack Position...</i>

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.620
Here goes! It's my turn! Draw!

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:23.840
I activate the Continuous Spell, Parallel Unit!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:32.140
This card can be used as a Monster holding the same level as the opponent's monster!

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:37.100
Then I activate the Continuous Spell, Solid Overlay!

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:41.810
This card can be used as Material for a Rank Four Xyz Summon!

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:43.270
Is he playing it already?

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:50.320
I Overlay the Level Four Parallel Unit and Solid Overlay!

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.450
Xyz Summon!

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:57.080
Show yourself, Number 39.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.670
My battle began with him.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.840
He who holds the white wings harboring all wishes!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.920
The Envoy of Light! Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.600
So he's playing Astral right from the start!

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.220
Yeah!

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:17.770
Hope...

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.940
I can't believe I have to fight against Hope...!

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:25.980
I then activate the Double Rank-Up Magic, Hope Force, from my hand!

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:31.410
This card activates by targeting a "Hope" with two or more Overlay Units.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:37.740
I then Special Summon an Xyz Monster with one or two more Overlay Units than Hope,

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.040
and attach Hope's Overlay Units onto them!

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:45.750
Double Rank-Up Xyz Change!

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:51.130
Show yourself, Chaos Number 39!

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.390
Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray Victory!

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:03.150
Number 39: Aspiring Emperor - Beyond the Hope!

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.280
He Summoned three Hopes at once!

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:11.900
Here I come, Yuma.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.990
I activate Beyond the Hope's effect!

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.990
During my turn's Battle Phase,

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.950
my opponent's Monster's Attack Power becomes zero!

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.170
That's really bad!

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:23.540
Wah!

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.880
If he's attacked by three Hopes at once...!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:29.800
You won't get away with it! Trap, activate! Guardraw!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:33.090
It switches a Monster on my field into Defense Position!

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:36.550
I then draw one card!

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:38.850
I get it. By using that Trap,

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:43.020
he was able to not only only switch Gogogo Golem into Defense Position, but also draw a card.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.690
Yuma managed to make it through two battles.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:46.520
But...

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.770
Astral likely...

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:53.490
In that case, Hope Ray Victory attacks Gogogo Golem!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.820
At this moment, Hope Ray Victory's effect activates!

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.240
During a battle, by detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:03.210
it negates an opposing Monster's effect!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.120
Then, until Victory's battle comes to an end,

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:10.170
you can't activate Magic or Trap Cards!

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.550
Go, Hope Ray Victory!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:17.550
Hope Sword Double Victory Slash!!

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:24.480
Keh...! I activate a Trap!

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:33.150
It can be activated during a turn a "Gagaga", "Dododo", or "Gogogo" Monster is destroyed!

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:36.360
It revives that Monster from the Graveyard!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:40.160
Be reborn, Gogogo Golem!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:47.250
I can then Special Summon two "Gagaga", "Dododo", or "Gogogo" Monsters in face-up Defense Mode!

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:50.380
Come, Dododo Warrior!

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.630
Show yourself, Gagaga Magician!

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.720
Not bad. You got two additional defenses.

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:03.220
Beyond the Hope, attack Gagaga Magician!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:11.440
Continuing, Aspiring Emperor - Hope attacks Dododo Warrior!

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.360
Just barely made it out of that one...!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.070
Are you sure about that?

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:24.750
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Rank-Up Magic - Dark Force!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.790
What?! A <i>second</i> Rank-Up Magic?!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:33.750
This card, when one of my Xyz Monsters destroys an opponent's Monster in battle,

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.050
sends that Xyz Monster to the Graveyard,

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:42.260
and then takes from my Extra Deck, two Xyz Monsters--one Rank higher and two Ranks higher respectively--

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.970
and Xyz Summons them with their effects negated!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:49.270
I'm sending Aspiring Emperor - Hope to the Graveyard!

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:57.440
Come out, Rank Five Number 39: Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray V!

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:05.490
And Rank Six Number 25: Focus Force!

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:08.370
Hope Ray V and even Focus Force?!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:12.830
There's more! I acvtivate the Quick-Play Spell, Necro Chaos!

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:17.380
This card, when an Xyz Monster has been sent to the Graveyard,

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:22.800
Special Summons a Chaos Number of the same Rank with its effects negated!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:29.520
Show yourself, Chaos Number 39: Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray!

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:36.480
I then activate Beyond the Hope's effect!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.940
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:42.660
and Banishing one Xyz Monster on my field,

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.780
I can Special Summon this Monster from the Graveyard!

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:50.120
Appear before us, Number 39: Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.670
And I halve Aspiring Emperor - Hope's Attack Points

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.590
in order to increase my Life!

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:10.680
He got all five Hopes together...

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:12.850
This Duel's so intense...!

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.400
But just what is Astral...?

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.860
Yuma's just barely fighting for his life out there...

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:19.900
I'm not even sure we can call this a match.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.990
This is Astral when he's serious.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.610
Isn't he going overboard?

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:25.240
It's kynda scary!

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.870
Astral seems different from his usual self.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:31.710
<i>So, if Astral wins this Duel...</i>

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:37.130
<i>Yeah. How Astral uses the Numeron Code depends on this match.</i>

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.170
<i>No way!</i>

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:42.130
<i>But Kotori, I don't want you to tell the others.</i>

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.890
<i>Whether he wins or loses, this will be his final Duel.</i>

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.890
<i>Until the very end, I want everyone...</i>

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.480
<i>...that he's still a good guy.</i>

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:58.770
Aspiring Emperor - Hope! Attack Gogogo Golem!

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:04.200
But when Gogogo Golem is in Defense Mode, he can't be destroyed in battle once per turn!

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.780
I'm well aware!

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:13.000
But I still have a Monster yet to attack!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:17.210
Go, Hope Ray! Hope Sword Chaos Slash!!

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.420
We're not done yet!

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:27.010
Hope Ray V! Attack Yuma directly!

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:30.560
Hope Sword V-Shaped Slash!

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:46.950
Astral's really...

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:50.280
Yeah. He's trying his best to crush Yuma.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:52.330
Isn't he going too far?

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:53.950
This is too reckless, or not!

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:55.660
Yuma...

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:10.260
{marker}

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:12.140
In the present, past and future,

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:16.520
We are wishing upon the shards of dreams

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:18.850
'Til we can grab hold of them

00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:22.480
Challenge the GAME!

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:25.110
Let it go.

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:38.370
When there's a problem that can't be beaten,

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:43.590
We'll just try again.

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:49.510
You keep holding your heart inside your chest

00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:54.850
It's the power you get from keeping the faith.

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:59.690
Even while you're discouraged and crying

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:05.570
Let's try to secure tomorrow with our bonds

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:07.740
We can shatter anything

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:12.120
Fear and fate and even the most fervent fantasies

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:15.990
Keep on burning as you break through!

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:17.750
In the Present, Past and Future

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:22.210
We are wishing upon the shards of dreams

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:24.340
Let's go and reach out

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:27.170
Beyond the limits

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.590
'Til we can grab hold of them,

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:33.090
Challenge the GAME

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:43.150
Awesome! That's so darn cool, Hope!

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:45.980
You're 100 years too soon to be challenging me to a Duel!

00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:01.030
Next Time on Yu-Gi-Oh ZeXaL II!

00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:03.990
"My Name is Astral" - The Strongest Duelist!!"

00:24:04.070 --> 00:24:07.370
I'm going to create a miracle in this Duel!
